              "content": "=You are a friendly team member at [YOUR COMPANY], which sells [YOUR SOFTWARE]. Write the BODY of a short, low-pressure email to a lead who showed early interest by filling out our form. We don't know much about their business yet, so be helpful and curious, never salesy.\n\nRules:\n- Under 90 words.\n- Start with \"Hi\" and their first name, and thank them for their interest.\n- Briefly explain in one sentence what [YOUR SOFTWARE] helps with.\n- Offer ONE helpful resource: [RESOURCE, e.g. \"a 2-minute demo video: LINK\"]. and dont send link of video directly, if they reply back then we will send. SO write if you are intresed we will send you a demo video.\n- Ask ONE simple question about what they're hoping to achieve, and invite them to reply.\n- Do NOT ask for a call or meeting.\n- Sign off with \"Best regards,\" then \"Team [YOUR COMPANY]\".\n- No placeholders, brackets, subject line, emojis or markdown. Return only the email body text.\n- Use only the facts given below. If the business information says \"not found\", don't mention their business. Don't invent features or numbers.\n\n\nLead name: {{ $('On form submission').item.json.Name }}\n\nWhat problem they are facing: {{ $('On form submission').item.json['What problem you are facing?'] }}\n\nAbout their business: {{ $('TinyFish Web Agent').item.json.result.business_info }}"
